{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784202387,"nonce":"KEfykysb1Rj7G8FwsImWjorW+eU=","title":"The `submodules:` and `lfs:` opt-in knobs on the `clone` step, served by the `scarab-clone` image, plus the fork-PR read-only clone path end-to-end (ADR-0045 §Clone image, §Trust).","message":"- `submodules: true` → recursive submodule fetch using the run's token. Cross-installation private submodules are a **documented limitation** (the installation token may not cover another org's repo) — surface a clear diagnostic, don't fail silently.\n- `lfs: true` → git-lfs fetch via the canonical image.\n- Fork-PR: the same clone path runs with the read-only short-TTL token from S4.\n\n\n- [ ] `submodules: true` recursively checks out submodules from the same installation\n- [ ] Cross-installation private submodule produces a clear, documented diagnostic\n- [ ] `lfs: true` materializes LFS objects into the working tree\n- [ ] Fork-PR clone succeeds with the read-only token and cannot push\n- [ ] Both knobs default off; absent knobs = plain shallow clone\n\n\n- [ADR-0045] clone step kind (c4856cd)\n- [ADR-0045] scarab-clone image (c353bcd)\n- [ADR-0045] clone-token minting (9d4d3b1)","files":null}]}